// Alert 1 — an anonymous request that SUCCEEDED.
//
// Backs ARD-039 §4 (the container is private) and KAT-417 T-002's boot refusal.
// After that refusal this should be **structurally impossible**: the API will not
// start against a publicly accessible container. A row here therefore means one of
// exactly two things, and the runbook says which to check first:
//
//   1. the container's access level was changed under an already-running pod, or
//   2. the boot check has a hole.
//
// Anonymous *failures* are deliberately excluded. The internet knocks on every
// storage endpoint it can enumerate; 404s and 403s from anonymous callers are
// weather, not signal. Only a 2xx means someone anonymous actually got bytes.
StorageBlobLogs
| where AuthenticationType == "Anonymous"
| where StatusCode >= 200 and StatusCode < 300
| project
    TimeGenerated,
    AccountName,
    OperationName,
    StatusCode,
    StatusText,
    CallerIpAddress,
    UserAgentHeader,
    ObjectKey,
    Uri
